  "body": "Add synthetic test fixtures for XYUV wire EDM swallowtails in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/`.\n\n## Context\n\nIssue #2690 asks for XYUV swallowtail test shapes before any healing code lands. Today `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ruled_tests.rs` tests folding notches and square-to-round punches, but has no dedicated fixtures for local or global swallowtails across disagreeing planes.\n\n## What this does\n\nAdd deterministic synthetic tests in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/` covering:\n\n- Local inside-corner swallowtails (`R = 0` and `0 < R < k`) on one plane and on both planes.\n- Global swallowtails: a dead-end narrow slot (`< 2k`) bridged by `Region::offset_sharp` and refused by `laws::cover`.\n- Global multi-loop splits: a narrow `Die` waist (`< 2k`) and a `Punch` keyhole cavity refused by `ring::wire_ring`.\n- Plane disagreement: one plane with a sharp corner or narrow slot while the other plane keeps an open fillet.\n- Mid-height ruling crossings and folds (`ruled_laws::folds` and `ruled_laws::crossing`) triggered by asymmetric profiles.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- Synthetic test fixtures in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/` cover all five cases above and pin the exact current refusal reasons (`laws::cover`, `ring::wire_ring`, `ruled_laws::folds`, `ruled_laws::crossing`).\n- `cargo xtask gate test wire_edm --crate camcraft-motion` passes.\n\nPart of #2690\n",
